## The man from Zundert

Question => Which Dutch town was Vincent van Gogh born in?
Answers => Zundert
Type => Open
AlsoAccept => Groot-Zundert
Grading => normalized
Hints => It sits in North Brabant, close to the Belgian border.
Explanation => Zundert, 30 March 1853. His father was the local minister.
Category => Life
Sources => https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vincent_van_Gogh

Question => Vincent's parents had a stillborn son exactly a year before Vincent was born. What first name did they give both boys?
Answers => Vincent
Type => Open
Grading => normalized
Hints => It is the name at the top of this quiz.
Explanation => Vincent. The first Vincent was buried in the churchyard at Zundert. The second got the name a year later, which is either touching or grim. Probably both.

Question => How many years older was Vincent than his brother Theo?
Answers => 4
Type => Range
Range => 0
Unit => years
Explanation => Vincent was born in 1853, Theo in 1857. Theo died six months after him.

Question => Which painting is this? It was his first major work.
Media => media/potato-eaters.jpg { alt="Five peasants around a table eating potatoes under a hanging lamp", credit="Van Gogh Museum, Amsterdam" }
Answers => The Potato Eaters
Type => Open
AlsoAccept => Potato Eaters | De Aardappeleters
Grading => normalized
Hints => He painted it in Nuenen, where his parents lived.
Explanation => The Potato Eaters, 1885. Five peasants, one lamp, no pretty colours. He was proud of it.
Category => Paintings

Question => Before he settled on painting, Vincent trained for another job. Which one?
Answers => Preacher | Doctor | Architect
Type => Choice
Correct => Preacher
Explanation => A lay preacher in the Borinage, a coal-mining region in Belgium. He gave most of his belongings away and the church let him go.

## The Yellow House

Question => Which French city did Vincent move to in February 1888?
Answers => Arles
Type => Open
Grading => normalized
Hints => It is in Provence, on the Rhône.
Explanation => Arles. In May he rented four rooms at 2 Place Lamartine, the building he painted yellow.
Category => Places

Question => Where did Vincent paint this café?
Media => media/cafe-terrace.jpg { alt="A café terrace at night under a yellow awning, with a starry sky above", credit="Kröller-Müller Museum, Otterlo" }
Answers => Arles | Paris | Auvers
Type => Choice
Correct => Arles
Explanation => Café Terrace at Night, September 1888. It is the Place du Forum in Arles, and the café is still there.
Category => Paintings

Question => In October 1888, the painter Paul [blank] came to stay.
Answers => Gauguin
Type => Cloze
Hints => He left for Tahiti a few years later.
Explanation => Paul Gauguin. Vincent had painted sunflowers for his room.

Question => After a quarrel with Gauguin in December 1888, Vincent cut off part of what?
Answers => his ear
Type => Open
AlsoAccept => ear | his left ear | left ear
Reject => his nose | his finger | his hand
Grading => normalized
Hints => It is on the side of your head.
Notes => Keep it light. Someone at every table knows the whole story and wants to tell it.
Explanation => Part of his left ear. He gave the piece to a woman at a local brothel. The exact sequence is still argued about.

Question => Match each painting to the place where Vincent painted it.
Type => Match
#### Answers
The Potato Eaters ~ Nuenen
Sunflowers ~ Arles
The Starry Night ~ Saint-Rémy
Wheatfield with Crows ~ Auvers
Score => 4
Explanation => Nuenen, Arles, Saint-Rémy, Auvers. Four stops, six years.

Question => Which of these did Vincent paint in Arles? Pick all that apply.
Answers => Sunflowers | The Starry Night | Café Terrace at Night | The Bedroom
Type => Choice
Multiple => true
Correct => Sunflowers | Café Terrace at Night | The Bedroom
Scoring => partial
Score => 3
Explanation => The Starry Night came later, at Saint-Rémy. The other three are from 1888 and from Arles.

## The studio

Question => Vincent painted this from the window of his room. Where was that room?
Media => media/starry-night.jpg { alt="A swirling night sky above a small village, with a tall dark cypress in the foreground", credit="Museum of Modern Art, New York" }
Answers => Saint-Rémy-de-Provence
Type => Open
AlsoAccept => Saint-Rémy | Saint Remy | Saint-Rémy de Provence | Saint Paul de Mausole | the asylum
Grading => normalized
Steps => media | fade | question | hints
Hints => It is a town in Provence, and he was in an asylum there.
Explanation => Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, June 1889. He painted the view before sunrise. The village below came from memory.
Category => Paintings
ColorScheme => night

Question => Which museum keeps The Starry Night?
Answers => MoMA | Musée d'Orsay | Van Gogh Museum
Type => Choice
Correct => MoMA
Explanation => The Museum of Modern Art in New York, since 1941. It rarely leaves the building.
Sources => https://www.moma.org/collection/works/79802

Question => Click the two people walking by the water.
Media => media/starry-night-rhone.jpg { alt="A starry night over a wide river, with gaslights reflected in the water and a couple walking on the bank", credit="Musée d'Orsay, Paris" }
Answers => 77,84
Type => Hotspot
HitRadius => 7
Score => 2
Explanation => Bottom right, arm in arm. The painting is Starry Night Over the Rhône, from September 1888.
Category => Paintings

Question => In February 1890, Vincent painted [blank] blossom for his newborn nephew.
Media => media/almond-blossom.jpg { alt="White blossom on twisting branches against a turquoise sky", credit="Van Gogh Museum, Amsterdam" }
Answers => almond
Type => Cloze
Hints => It is the first tree to flower in spring.
Explanation => Almond blossom. Theo's son was called Vincent Willem, after his uncle.

Question => True or false about The Starry Night?
Answers => True | False
Rows => It hangs in New York | It shows a cypress tree | Vincent sold it in his lifetime
Correct => True | True | False
Type => Matrix
Score => 3
Explanation => MoMA, yes. The cypress, yes. Sold in his lifetime, no. He never saw a buyer for that one.

## A picture round

RoundTimer => 6m

Question => Name this painting.
Media => media/sunflowers.jpg { alt="A vase of sunflowers against a pale blue-green background", credit="Neue Pinakothek, Munich" }
Answers => Sunflowers
Type => Open
AlsoAccept => Vase with Twelve Sunflowers | Still Life: Vase with Twelve Sunflowers | Zonnebloemen
Grading => normalized
Hints => There are twelve of them.
Explanation => Sunflowers, August 1888. The Munich version, with twelve flowers and a blue-green wall. He painted it for Gauguin's room.
Category => Paintings

Question => In which year did Vincent paint this bedroom?
Media => media/bedroom.jpg { alt="A blue bedroom with a wooden bed, two chairs, a table and framed pictures on the wall", credit="Van Gogh Museum, Amsterdam" }
Answers => 1888
Type => Range
Range => 1
Unit => year
Hints => The same year he moved to Arles.
Explanation => October 1888. He made three versions. He wanted the colours to say rest, or sleep.

Question => What was this building called?
Media => media/yellow-house.jpg { alt="A yellow corner house under a deep blue sky, with a shop and a café on the street", credit="Van Gogh Museum, Amsterdam" }
Answers => The Yellow House
Type => Open
AlsoAccept => The Yellow House (The Street) | Het gele huis | Yellow House
Grading => normalized
Hints => The quiz is named after it.
Explanation => The Yellow House at 2 Place Lamartine, Arles. It was damaged in 1944 and later pulled down. The painting is all that is left.
Category => Places

Question => Which birds are flying over the field?
Media => media/wheatfield-crows.jpg { alt="A wide golden wheatfield under a dark blue sky, with a flock of black birds", credit="Van Gogh Museum, Amsterdam" }
Answers => Crows | Swallows | Pigeons
Type => Choice
Correct => Crows
Explanation => Crows. Wheatfield with Crows, July 1890, Auvers. People call it his last painting. Nobody actually knows.
Category => Paintings

Question => Which of these is in the Musée d'Orsay?
Answers => media/self-portrait.jpg { alt="A self-portrait with a red beard against a pale swirling blue background" } | media/starry-night.jpg { alt="A swirling night sky above a village" } | media/sunflowers.jpg { alt="A vase of sunflowers" }
Type => Choice
Correct => media/self-portrait.jpg { alt="A self-portrait with a red beard against a pale swirling blue background" }
Explanation => The 1889 self-portrait. The Starry Night is at MoMA, and this version of Sunflowers is in Munich.

## The afterlife

Question => Which 1971 song by Don McLean opens with "Starry, starry night"?
Answers => Vincent | American Pie | Cinnamon Girl
Type => Choice
Correct => Vincent
Explanation => "Vincent", also known as "Starry, Starry Night". It reached number one in the UK.
Category => Legacy

Question => Which Amsterdam museum is devoted to his work?
Answers => Van Gogh Museum
Type => Open
AlsoAccept => The Van Gogh Museum | Van Gogh Museum Amsterdam
Reject => Rijksmuseum
Grading => normalized
Explanation => The Van Gogh Museum, opened in 1973. Theo's family kept the collection together, which is why it is all in one place.
Category => Legacy

Question => Put each person in the right box.
Type => Classification
#### Answers
Theo van Gogh
Jo van Gogh-Bonger
Paul Gauguin
Doctor Gachet
Buckets => Family | Fellow painter | Doctor
Correct => Theo van Gogh @ Family | Jo van Gogh-Bonger @ Family | Paul Gauguin @ Fellow painter | Doctor Gachet @ Doctor
Score => 4
Explanation => Theo was his brother and dealer. Jo was Theo's wife, and she got the paintings seen. Gachet looked after Vincent in Auvers.

Question => About how many oil paintings did Vincent make in his ten working years?
Answers => 860
Type => Estimate
Tolerance => 60
Unit => paintings
Slider => 700..1000
Score => 2
Explanation => Around 860 oil paintings, plus about 1,300 drawings and watercolours. Ten years of work.

Question => Put these paintings in the order Vincent painted them, oldest first.
Answers => The Potato Eaters | Sunflowers | The Starry Night | Wheatfield with Crows
Type => Sort
Correct => The Potato Eaters | Sunflowers | The Starry Night | Wheatfield with Crows
Score => 4
Explanation => 1885, 1888, 1889, 1890. The last one is from the final weeks.

Question => How many months after Vincent did his brother Theo die?
Answers => 6
Type => Range
Range => 1
Unit => months
Timer => 1:30
Wager => true
Notes => Take the bets before you reveal. Nothing focuses a room like a wager.
Hints => Not years. Months.
Explanation => Vincent died on 29 July 1890. Theo died on 25 January 1891, less than six months later, aged 33.

Type => End
